WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.050
French girl.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.770
The first projectile was a fake.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.910
This is my real weapon...

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.530
Ash to ash!

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.280
No! That arrow is...

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.080
Ashes to ashes.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.530
Those who should die 
should head to realm of the dead.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.790
Die, Jeanne.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.450
Don't!

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.110
She lost her heart,

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.140
and her wound from 
the Holy Lance isn't healing.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.270
But her head was not destroyed.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.380
If she's not dead, then there 
must be a way to save her.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.000
Isn't that right, Astaroth?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.030
Yes.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.100
We will retrieve the Escalibor.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.030
The mystic sword Escalibor.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.370
It is a Philosopher's Stone with
 outstanding healing properties.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.750
Perhaps if we use it...

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.130
Um...

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.050
I thought the mystic sword Escalibor

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.720
belonged to the legendary 
knight, Roi Arthur?

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.030
Yes, he is known as King Arthur in England.

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:33.140
Legend has it the king returned Escalibor 
to Fairy of the Lake prior to his death.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.030
How did it end up in France? 
In a forest like this?

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.300
To be more accurate, we're not 
searching for the sword itself.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.600
We're looking for its scabbard.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.810
Its scabbard?

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:50.260
It's too dangerous to keep the 
powerful sword and scabbard together.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.120
That's why I hid the scabbard in this forest.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.300
Wait a minute! Does that 
mean the Fairy of the Lake is...

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.180
You've been alive for a thousand years?!

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.060
Even longer.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.800
Are you going to tell me that you saw
the great flood in the Book of Genesis,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.180
with your own eyes, too?

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.800
What? Really?

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.030
You've seen it?!

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.250
What about Noah's Ark?

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.610
Enough idle talk!

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.240
It's too distracting.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.280
It's not really idle talk...

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.500
I don't...

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.970
think it is...

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.090
<i>Lord, please protect Orléans.</i>

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:50.310
<b>#08 Return of the Female Saint</b>

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.550
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.280
Just wait, Jeanne.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.150
We'll revive you real soon.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:26.090
Although, we'll be lying 
next to her if we screw up.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:32.540
Men! It's showtime!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.520
Regroup!

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.110
We can take down the fortress 
if we get through this!

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.480
Where are the Escalibor 
and the reinforcements?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.340
I didn't think it would 
take so long to get here!

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.020
This is not what you told us!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.240
Don't tell me...

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.280
What do you expect? 
It was a thousand years ago!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.410
And you call yourself the queen of fairies?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.410
You, a mere human,
dares to question me?

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.540
Um... Can I say something?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.720
You stay out of this!

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.670
Okay!

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:25.630
Humans have such large bodies, 
but your brains are so small and dumb!

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.960
Does a fairy who forgot the 
location of the mystic sword

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.240
have any right to insult our brains?

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.440
As I thought! Look!

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.340
What? You're so annoying!

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.950
Those rocks moved to a different position!

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:39.420
No, they don't seem any different to me...

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.870
What is happening?

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.790
It's one of the traps 
I set up to prevent knights

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.840
from finding the scabbard.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.080
You forgot about this, too?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.840
Shut up!

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.500
Alençon, hold up the Philosopher's Stone.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.130
H-Huh?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.100
Idiot! Hurry and hold it up!

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:14.640
You fools! Can't you see 
the Philosopher's Stone?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.570
They stopped.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.150
What happened?

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.320
That's a Philosopher's Stone.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:30.110
But there's only half of it.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.090
What happened?

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.410
Fairies?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.990
The Korrigan Tribe.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.140
A thousand years ago, 
I ordered them to protect this forest.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.540
Wow!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.940
Gatekeepers, take us to the scabbard.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:45.770
A witch!

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:46.590
She's a witch!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.030
A witch is here!

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:50.050
You've all got the wrong idea!

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.210
You'd better not have forgotten me!

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.050
Who are you again?

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.420
I don't remember.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.880
Is she talking about our ancestors?

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:02.060
Keep memos for important things! 
You want to die?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.620
Are you the one to talk? Huh?

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:18.550
This way? That way? This way?

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.270
Huh?

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.500
Huh? What? Hmm?

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:24.960
That's strange.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:26.460
What's wrong?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.730
It's gone!

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.540
Huh?

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.000
Look, over there!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.760
Oh, you've found me!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.970
That was faster than I expected.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.350
Who are you?!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.300
I am Sir Thomas Malory.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:46.730
I'm the captain of Duke of Bedford's 
Philosopher's Stone Search Party.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.610
The English army's?!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:53.290
Tsk, tsk, tsk. I'm a princess 
knight of Wales, to be accurate.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.420
Do you know where Wales is?

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.870
It's a country at the edge 
of the Britain Island.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.670
It's been assimilated by England, though.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.250
Now I get it.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:04.900
What?

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.630
Wales is King Arthur's domain.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:12.670
It wouldn't be surprising if they 
had an ancient document or two

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.760
that showed the location of the scabbard.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.300
Correct!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.700
So Escalibor...

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:24.270
No, Excalibur's scabbard will 
be returned to where it belongs.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.520
No hard feelings.

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.530
I'll have to let the queen know!

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.080
Did you know?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:39.130
The longbow was originally 
developed by the Wales army

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:42.200
to defeat the English cavalry units.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.790
Enough with the futile 
resistance, and get down here!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.170
We'll spare you if you 
hand over the scabbard.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.300
Do you think you can stay up there forever?

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:53.900
My queen!

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.680
Knights are heading this way!

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.250
There's at least a hundred of them!

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.690
What?!

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:01.290
That's how it is.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:05.070
You will be terminated by my 
Philosopher's Stone Search Party,

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:07.200
and then I will get down 
from this tree with dignity,

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.730
and take back the scabbard.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:13.560
Oh, there's still the option of 
running with tails between your legs.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.450
What are you going to do?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.860
<i>There's no way we can 
defeat a hundred knights.</i>

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:19.580
<i>But...</i>

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:21.660
<i>without the scabbard,</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.940
<i>we can't revive Jeanne.</i>

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:26.760
<i>If that were to happen, 
Montmorency would...</i>

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.960
Batard, distract her.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:32.710
Huh?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.970
O-Okay.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:41.350
Hey, if you don't get down soon, 
I'll light the tree on fire!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.630
No! You'll burn down the whole forest!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.750
I'm gonna get rid of the 
evil princess knight!

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:50.220
Are you serious?!

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.740
I'm serious!

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:51.740
Hey!

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:56.520
My Search Party will arrive 
before this tree burns down.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:00.000
I doubt you're stupid enough not to know that.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.490
Yet you tre to draw my attention, for...

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.010
Distraction!

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.500
That's the answer!

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.880
Astaroth!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:23.290
It's really unfortunate that we've lost

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.470
a thousand years of vault information!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:30.420
I wanted to catch you, and keep 
you forever in an iron cage!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.870
What's so funny?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.440
The fairy queen can't die.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:45.660
Not even if she wanted to.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.120
The protector of the Philosopher's Stone
 is destined to be revived,

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.420
no matter how many 
thousands of times she dies.

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.590
Over there!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.740
I'm not pleased about taking a woman hostage,

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:03.210
but it will buy us time.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:05.180
You two go ahead.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.260
We can't do that!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:10.920
The revival of the maiden will 
greatly boost the soldiers' morale.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.460
That scabbard must be delivered to Orléans,

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.000
no matter the cost.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.490
What are you gonna do?

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.980
What will you do?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.100
Let's go.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.110
That way!

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:28.950
Hurry!

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:32.460
Alençon!

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.950
Alençon died a glorious 
death as a knight in battle.

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:38.710
Spread the word if you're a true friend.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.900
This... is the way it should be.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:52.830
Wonderful swordsmanship, as expected 
of Lady Richemont's brother.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:56.700
Lady Richemont wouldn't have 
made a mistake like that.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:00.190
And you call yourself Arthur 
de Richemont's little brother?

00:12:23.030 --> 00:12:25.840
I was born with a destiny...

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.970
to surpass my older sister.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.700
I can finally surpass her.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:35.430
Everyone will finally approve of me.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.360
Montmorency!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:02.050
Astaroth!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:06.400
Batard carried Escalibor to Orléans.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.420
Great!

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.550
Where's Alençon?

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.140
Are you serious?

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.320
Commander Gilles, enemy troops ahead!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.780
I put all my fortune into forming this troop.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:36.480
If Orléans were to be liberated,

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:39.230
the Princess would head to Reims.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:43.840
I would never again have an 
opportunity for a truce with England.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.680
You're such a nuisance, defeatist!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.760
This is the official army 
of the royal family.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.900
You're nothing more than a rebel 
for trying to get in our way!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.040
This isn't the time 
to be fighting La Tremoille.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.100
We have to get to Orléans 
as soon as possible...

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.840
<i>I won't let you become the heroic savior.</i>

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.340
<i>I'm the one who will save France.</i>

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:11.620
I hear that fake savior 
named Jeanne is dead...

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:17.510
By having her heart squeezed 
in the most gruesome manner.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:22.630
A fitting death for a wretched witch!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.580
Don't let him provoke you.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.470
You punk.

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:31.820
You're not worthy of saying Jeanne's name.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.140
I'll kill you!

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:36.690
Yeah, that's the look.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.970
You're not a hero.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.150
That's your true face.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.320
Montmorency!

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.140
Alençon!

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:49.280
You're safe!

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.650
I'm not alone.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.420
Th-That military force...

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.430
It's my sister's private army.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:18.910
All troops, pull back!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.440
We're making a tactical withdrawal!

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:37.140
I came here after hearing reports of English 
troops secretly traveling in our territory.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.910
I didn't expect to find you here.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:49.240
I'm back to being the laughing stock again.

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:53.590
I made the grand gesture of sacrificing 
myself to let my friends live,

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.810
and in the end, I was saved by my older sister.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:58.280
I'm...

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.360
I'm such a...

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:07.190
I won't laugh.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.270
You've done well, Alençon.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.260
I'm so proud of you.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.840
I see...

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:19.310
I didn't want to be acknowledged by everyone.

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:22.090
I wanted to be acknowledged by you.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.800
Facing a traitor's troops 
after fighting enemy troops.

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.890
There isn't a moment 
of boredom for us, is there?

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.160
Montmorency.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:36.390
You must not get distracted by a loser 
like him and forget who you are.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:41.560
Arthur de Richemont hereby 
declares battle on the basis

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.890
of personal grudge with La Tremoille!

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:46.650
Our enemy is La Tremoille!

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.490
Ignore Montmorency's troops 
and let them through.

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:53.150
I repeat, this is a fight to the death!

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:54.800
Wait, Richemont!

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.150
We can handle this as the official 
army of the royal family!

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:00.720
Fight to the death or not, 
this will put you in a difficult positionー

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.160
Go, Montmorency.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.200
If you're a true knight, 
you must not let Jeanne die.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.220
Don't look at me like that.

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:15.900
I'm a bit too strong to be a princess 
protected by a knight in shining armor.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:30.980
<i>Montmorency, you must become a true knight.</i>

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.760
Hey, Astaroth...

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:38.920
I was forgiven by Catherine, 
and saved by Richemont.

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:43.450
Will I become a man 
who can protect them one day?

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.400
Will you become?

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.080
You must.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.410
Montmorency...

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.100
Montmorency...

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:11.320
Where are you?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.140
Montmorency!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.370
Hey, Batard!

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:20.370
Alençon!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.060
You're alive!

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:23.100
I'm so gladー

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.330
We can talk later.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.750
How's the battle going?

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:27.630
It's only getting worse.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:31.130
They're managing to hold for now, 
but it's just a matter of time.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:38.660
We'll have a chance to win, 
if Montmorency can reach Jeanne.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:41.990
Open a path for him!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:47.390
I don't like girls, but if 
we're facing male knights...

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:49.030
Montmorency.

00:18:49.030 --> 00:18:51.150
Yeah, let's go!

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:02.300
I'm scared...

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.780
I'm lonely.

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.420
I'm all alone.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.300
Montmorency...

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.540
Montmorency!

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:30.560
Jeanne!

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:43.990
Montmorency is coming.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:48.620
Not to me, but to the white Ulysses.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:03.160
What's going on?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:08.600
The elixir is drying up inside her, 
so the scabbard is not reacting.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.350
Montmorency, hurry and let her drink elixir.

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:18.110
The cursed princess will wake up 
with the prince's baiser.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.740
It's working!

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.900
Montmorency...

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:50.390
It took me a little too much time, 
but I'm here to wake you.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:02.750
I can tell by the smell 
that it's you, Montmorency.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:06.060
Sorry, I didn't have time to take a bath.

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:07.410
It's all right.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:10.300
Let me be like this for a while longer.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.960
Enemy reinforcements are 2,000 men strong!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.420
They're taking one point of strategic 
importance after another!

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.540
Commander Campbell died in battle!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:27.640
We've received a report that the black 
alchemist already entered the fortress!

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:30.870
Glasdale?

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.180
How's your wound?

00:21:34.180 --> 00:21:35.520
It's fine.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.640
As long as I have the Holy Grail,

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:42.470
I can never be blessed with death.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.030
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>#09 Dance Music of White and Black</b>

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:23.250
The white and the black are to meet once again.

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:25.750
Finally, a conclusion to the 
battle between the two Ulysses.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.280
Will the small or the big win?

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:29.010
I mean, the white or the black?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:31.510
Episode 9: 'Dance Music of White and Black."

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:34.100
This time around, I can 
only cheer for the small!

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>"Are you serious?!"</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Use it to someone who is going insane!</b>
